- Preserve the existing read-only GitLab access.
- Never expose the raw PAT in prompts, chat, console, logs, API responses or UI.
- Distinguish TOKEN_MISSING, TOKEN_INVALID/EXPIRED and GITLAB_UNREACHABLE correctly.
- Do not report TOKEN_MISSING when a saved token actually exists.

Verify end-to-end:
Connect & Test succeeds → start mim-expert → ask it to inspect an allowed GitLab repository → it must successfully read the code using the same saved PAT.

Fix the root cause, not just the displayed error.



